IMPORT prelude

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in plain days ("within 30 days of the grant", "for at least 30 days")
-- and in months ("within 6 months after the date of the grant", "within 3 months of the date of the right to elect notice").
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Administration
-- and Probate Act 1958, Version No. 130 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Administration and Probate Act 1958`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The earlier of two days.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day` THEN `the first day` ELSE `the second day`

-- The later of two days.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is after` `the second day` THEN `the first day` ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month a number of months on; where that month is shorter, its last day (fork F1 in NOTES.md). This is
-- the last day of a period of n months counted from a day, the day itself excluded.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1
